---
// Themed (light/dark aware) "ceiling" diagram for Day 24: a better model
// raises the top bar, but the actual output quality is capped by the data
// quality bar underneath it, whichever is lower.
---

<div class="dcd">
  <div class="dcd__bars">
    <div class="dcd__bar-group">
      <div class="dcd__bar dcd__bar--model" style="--h: 92%;">
        <span class="dcd__bar-label">Model quality</span>
      </div>
      <p class="dcd__bar-caption">High</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dcd__bar-group">
      <div class="dcd__bar dcd__bar--data" style="--h: 38%;">
        <span class="dcd__bar-label">Data quality</span>
      </div>
      <p class="dcd__bar-caption">Low</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dcd__bar-group">
      <div class="dcd__bar dcd__bar--output" style="--h: 38%;">
        <span class="dcd__bar-label">What users actually get</span>
      </div>
      <p class="dcd__bar-caption">Capped</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="dcd__ceiling" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <p class="dcd__note">
    A better model raises the model-quality bar. It does not raise the ceiling set by the
    data underneath it — the real output stays capped at the lower of the two.
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  .dcd {
    margin: 1.6em 0;
    padding: 22px 20px 18px;
    border: 2px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .dcd__bars {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    align-items: end;
    gap: 18px;
    height: 180px;
    position: relative;
  }

  .dcd__bar-group {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    height: 100%;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .dcd__bar {
    width: 100%;
    height: var(--h);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0 0;
    border: 1px solid;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: center;
    padding-top: 8px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .dcd__bar--model {
    background: rgba(124, 58, 237, 0.16);
    border-color: rgba(124, 58, 237, 0.45);
  }

  .dcd__bar--data {
    background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.14);
    border-color: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.45);
  }

  .dcd__bar--output {
    background: rgba(107, 114, 128, 0.18);
    border-color: rgba(107, 114, 128, 0.5);
  }

  .dcd__bar-label {
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .dcd__bar-caption {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--mute);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  .dcd__ceiling {
    position: relative;
    margin-top: -68px;
    margin-bottom: 46px;
    height: 2px;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(
      to right,
      var(--blue) 0,
      var(--blue) 8px,
      transparent 8px,
      transparent 14px
    );
  }

  .dcd__note {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--sub);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .dcd__bars {
      height: 150px;
    }
    .dcd__ceiling {
      margin-top: -56px;
      margin-bottom: 38px;
    }
  }
</style>
